---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal
  title="Terms"
  description="How Final Commit works with students: the quote, the payment stages, changes, exclusivity, plagiarism, ownership and support."
  updated="7 October 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms cover every project we build with a student. They're written in plain English on purpose. If anything here is unclear,
    ask us on WhatsApp at {site.phone} before you pay anything.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Final Commit is run by two software developers in India. We build software projects with final-year and mini-project students, and
    prepare them to explain and defend the work. Contact: WhatsApp or call {site.phone}, or email {site.email}.
  </p>

  <h2>Your part, and academic integrity</h2>
  <p>
    We build the project with you and teach you every part of it, so you can explain it in your reviews and your viva. You're
    responsible for following your college's rules on outside help. We won't attend a review, a viva or an exam on your behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>The quote</h2>
  <p>
    After a free call you get a written quote with the scope, the tech stack, the deliverables and the dates. Once you accept it, the
    price doesn't change. If you later ask for something outside that scope, we agree the extra time and cost with you in writing
    before doing it.
  </p>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>You pay</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Free call, written quote and synopsis</td><td>₹0</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Your guide approves the synopsis</td><td>30%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Working demo on a video call</td><td>40%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Setup on your laptop, code walkthrough and mock viva</td><td>30%</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Smaller jobs on a project you've already started (fixes, new features, the report, viva prep) get a written quote the same way,
    and you pay after you've seen the work: in one go for a small job, or in stages for a bigger one.
  </p>
  <p>
    You pay each part only after that stage is done. You get a receipt for every payment. We take UPI or bank transfer. We will never
    ask you for an OTP, a password, or to install a remote-control app.
  </p>

  <h2>Building and seeing the work</h2>
  <p>
    Your project is built in a private GitHub repository that you can see from the first day. You get a working demo before each review
    your college holds.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    Small changes your guide asks for are included until your final submission. If the whole idea changes halfway, we agree a new
    timeline, and any change in price, in writing first.
  </p>

  <h2>Exclusivity</h2>
  <p>We never build the same project for two students from the same college and batch.</p>

  <h2>Plagiarism</h2>
  <p>
    Your report is written for your project, not copied from another report. If your college's similarity check (for example DrillBit,
    Turnitin or URKUND) flags it above the college's limit, send us the check report and we rewrite the flagged parts free.
  </p>

  <h2>Ownership</h2>
  <p>
    Once the final payment is made, the code and documents we made for your project are yours. We keep a private copy only to support
    you, and we never publish your project or show it to other students without your permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    We host your project free, with a live link, until your viva. If you want your own domain or an always-on server, you pay the
    provider directly at their price; we don't add anything on top.
  </p>

  <h2>Support</h2>
  <p>
    Until your viva: help getting the demo running before reviews, reinstallation if your laptop changes, answers about your code on
    WhatsApp, and a mock viva. We reply on WhatsApp between {site.hours.toLowerCase()}.
  </p>

  <h2>If we can't deliver</h2>
  <p>
    If we can't deliver a stage, you don't pay for it, and if you've already paid for it you get that money back. The{' '}
    <a href="/refunds/">refund policy</a> has the details.
  </p>

  <h2>Law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India. If something goes wrong, talk to us first; we'd rather fix it.</p>
</Legal>
